Composition algebras, https://github.com/ehrlich-b/composition-algebras, commit
98d4437ce1bfd8d042b8383e0cfe28ec3e595eee (Palomar entry PALOMAR-2026-08-29-000018), Apache-2.0. Copyright holder as
stated in the retained upstream headers: Bryan Ehrlich ("Copyright (c) 2026 Bryan Ehrlich. All rights
reserved.", "Authors: Bryan Ehrlich"). The ten files under src/CompositionAlgebras (Composition/Defs, Composition/Doubling,
Composition/CayleyDickson, Composition/Instances, Composition/Isomorphisms, Composition/Hurwitz,
Composition/Classification, Octonions, OctonionTrace, OctonionModule) are adapted whole. The upstream archive SHA-256 is
707a08e715beb738eae294b87d67ffd06d530819e9f6038132a2d49a48fb0852. The upstream copyright and author
headers remain in all ten adapted Lean files under src/CompositionAlgebras. The exact upstream license is
src/CompositionAlgebras/LICENSE, SHA-256 cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30.
Upstream has no NOTICE file. Upstream used Lean v4.33.0 and Mathlib db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d.
The port uses Lean's module system, updates one deprecated Mathlib import in Octonions.lean and removes unused
tactic combinators and simp arguments in Composition/Isomorphisms.lean. The project pins remain at v4.36.0.
Thanks to Bryan Ehrlich.

